<!-- PROBLEM -->
<section id="problem">
  <div class="container problem-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Your stack has too many moving parts.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Every pipeline ends up stitched together from a warehouse, an orchestrator, a stream processor, a scheduler, and a pile of glue scripts. Quarry collapses the parts that do not need to be separate.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="problem-list">
      <li>
        <div class="x">01</div>
        <div>
          <h4>Load steps that never end</h4>
          <p>Copying data into a warehouse just to query it again doubles storage and adds latency. Quarry reads Parquet, Iceberg, and CSV where they live.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="x">02</div>
        <div>
          <h4>Clusters for small jobs</h4>
          <p>Spinning up infrastructure for a 200 MB transform is absurd. Quarry runs in-process on a laptop, a CI runner, or a Lambda, then scales out when you need it.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="x">03</div>
        <div>
          <h4>Two languages, two bugs</h4>
          <p>Business logic drifts between SQL models and Python scripts. Quarry lets you mix both against the same catalog, with the same types and tests.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

