<!-- FEATURES -->
<section id="features" style="padding-top:40px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Features</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Everything a pipeline needs.<br>Nothing it doesn't.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Built from the ground up for the workflows data engineers actually run every day.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="features">
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><ellipse cx="12" cy="6" rx="8" ry="3"/><path d="M4 6v12c0 1.7 3.6 3 8 3s8-1.3 8-3V6"/><path d="M4 12c0 1.7 3.6 3 8 3s8-1.3 8-3"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Query data in place</h3>
        <p>Read Parquet, Iceberg, Delta, Avro, and JSON directly from object storage. Predicate and projection pushdown keep scans cheap.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature">
        <div class="icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M13 2 3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Streaming ingest, no broker</h3>
        <p>Consume Kafka or Kinesis topics with exactly-once semantics and checkpointed state. Materialized views stay fresh without a separate stream processor.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature">
        <div class="icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M4 7h16M4 12h10M4 17h13"/><circle cx="19" cy="12" r="2"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>SQL and Python, together</h3>
        <p>Write models in SQL, then drop into Python with typed UDFs and DataFrame interop. Both run against the same catalog and the same optimizer.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature">
        <div class="icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Incremental by default</h3>
        <p>Quarry tracks which files changed and refreshes only the partitions that need it. Backfills are a single statement, not a weekend project.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature">
        <div class="icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M9 11l3 3 8-8"/><path d="M20 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Tests and contracts</h3>
        <p>Declare schemas, freshness SLAs, and data quality checks next to your models. Failing contracts block downstream refreshes before bad data spreads.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature">
        <div class="icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><circle cx="6" cy="6" r="2.5"/><circle cx="18" cy="6" r="2.5"/><circle cx="12" cy="18" r="2.5"/><path d="M6 8.5v2a3 3 0 0 0 3 3h6a3 3 0 0 0 3-3v-2M12 13.5v2"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Column-level lineage</h3>
        <p>Every column knows where it came from. Trace a broken dashboard metric back to the exact upstream field and commit that changed it.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

