<section style="padding-top:40px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head center">
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>Is Quarry production-ready?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Version 2.x is used in production by teams processing petabytes per day. Releases follow semantic versioning, and breaking changes are announced one minor version in advance.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How is Quarry different from DuckDB?</summary>
        <p>Quarry shares the embedded, in-process model, but adds streaming ingest, incremental materialized views, contracts, lineage, and a distributed execution mode for when one machine is not enough.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I use my existing Parquet and Iceberg tables?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Quarry reads them in place and never requires you to migrate data into a proprietary format. Writes use the standard table formats, so other engines can keep reading your data.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What license is it under?</summary>
        <p>Quarry is released under the Apache License 2.0. The core engine, CLI, Python client, and connectors are all open source. Managed hosting and enterprise support are optional.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I contribute?</summary>
        <p>Start with issues labeled <em>good first issue</em>, read CONTRIBUTING.md, and join our community chat. Connector development has its own guide and a template repository.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
